#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/pt.rc -- Portuguese (Brazil), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "pt"`.
//
// Stage L10N, task T-L10N-2: the two string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the
// menu block -- moved here out of app.rc unchanged; app.rc includes this file, and the built
// RT_STRING resource stayed byte for byte what it was. The rules every table obeys stand in
// app.rc above the #include lines; where each string is seen and how much room it has is
// res/lang/context.tsv; tests/l10n.rs holds this file to en.rc.
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Portuguese (Brazil) — `[general] language = "pt"`. LANG_PORTUGUESE 0x16 with
// SUBLANG_PORTUGUESE_BRAZILIAN 0x01, that is `pt-BR` and **not** the 0x0816 of Portugal.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LANGUAGE 0x16, 0x01
STRINGTABLE
